## browse

The plugin ships the **browse** binary, built and published by Anomaly (https://github.com/anomalyco/browse), MIT,
Copyright (c) 2025 opencode. It is not contained in this package: each platform package
(`@joe-broadhead/opencode-browse-bin-<platform>`) carries the pinned binary with its own `LICENSE.browse` and
`manifest/browse.json`, which records the release, the target, the binary's SHA-256 and its size. The pinned release
is recorded in `manifest/browse.json` in this package, with the upstream tarball's URL, SHA-256 and size.

The browse browser extension is not shipped or bundled. It is installed by the user from the Chrome Web Store, under
its own listing and terms, and it is licensed MIT by the same project.

## Nothing else

No other third-party code is bundled. The platform packages carry the binary and the licence text above, and nothing
else.
